# Hard Rules Verification Checklist — 6-STEP MANDATORY PIPELINE

Before marking ANY task as verified/complete, you MUST have a checklist entry
for each of the following. If ANY box is unchecked, the task is NOT done.

## Pre-verification checklist (run this EVERY time, for ALL tasks, no exceptions)

```
ISOLATED (do these FIRST, before ANY in-game test):
[ ] 1.  Isolated BEFORE screenshot on disk (pre-change state, isolated scene)
[ ] 2.  Isolated AFTER screenshot on disk (post-change state, isolated scene)
[ ] 3.  Isolated COMPARE — diff or side-by-side read, both images opened +
        concrete pixel differences stated in writing

IN-GAME (only after all 3 isolated steps are green):
[ ] 4.  In-game BEFORE screenshot on disk (pre-change state, real game)
[ ] 5.  In-game AFTER screenshot on disk (post-change state, real game)
[ ] 6.  In-game COMPARE — diff or side-by-side read, both images opened +
        concrete pixel differences stated in writing

FINALIZE:
[ ] 7.  ALL 6 screenshots read with the Read tool; described what is ACTUALLY shown
[ ] 8.  Report JSON verdict is PASS / expected fields match
[ ] 9.  PLAN.md status updated, referencing all 6 screenshot paths
[ ] 10. All 6+ screenshots + report JSONs committed to git and pushed
[ ] 11. App restarted with tools/restart_app.ps1 so user sees the change live
```

## How to use

1. Before starting a task, copy the checklist into your todo list.
2. Tick each box as you complete it. Do NOT start any in-game step until
   boxes 1–3 are all ticked.
3. If you cannot tick a box, the task is NOT done — note what is missing.
4. **Never** mark a task "verified" or "complete" in PLAN.md with any box unchecked.
5. **Never** skip the BEFORE screenshots. If you already made the code change,
   you MUST temporarily revert to capture the before state (both isolated AND in-game).
6. **Never** rely on the report JSON alone — you must open each PNG with the
   Read tool and describe what you see.
7. **Never** leave screenshots uncommitted. Run `git add tools/selftest/results/`
   and commit + push after every verification batch.

## Common mistakes to avoid

- Marking a task done based on "the report says PASS" without reading the screenshots.
- Skipping the isolated test and going straight to the full game.
- Capturing only an "after" screenshot without a "before" for comparison.
- Forgetting the COMPARE step: just having before+after is NOT enough; you must
  actually open both and state the visible difference.
- Forgetting to commit the result PNGs and report JSON to git.
- Not restarting the app at the end of the turn.
- Using a single screenshot to "verify" a multi-phase feature.
